WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.129
Local AI keeps selected processing close to users and private data.

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:13.541
It can provide low network latency, offline capability, direct control over versions, and predictable availability after hardware is purchased.

00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:21.542
These strengths suit confidential document review, local coding assistance, edge inference, and routine workloads that fit existing systems.

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:24.209
Cloud capacity complements those limits.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:35.493
A team can burst to larger GPUs for a temporary job, call a model with capabilities unavailable locally, or serve remote users without distributing high-end hardware.

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:39.802
Shared cloud services can support collaboration and centralized operations.

00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:47.803
The benefit appears when the cloud role is defined, not when every request is sent remotely by default.

00:00:47.803 --> 00:00:50.880
Hybrid designs can also provide alternatives.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:57.240
If a local server is unavailable, an approved cloud service may preserve non-sensitive workflows.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:04.831
If a hosted API fails or reaches a rate limit, a local model may provide reduced capability.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:12.012
Redundancy is real only when clients, authentication, model behavior, and data policy support the alternate path.

00:01:12.012 --> 00:01:17.962
A fallback that cannot accept the same data is not a transparent substitute.

00:01:17.962 --> 00:01:24.322
Using both environments reduces dependence on a single architecture but adds integration and operations.

00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:30.682
Teams must manage model differences, APIs, identities, network paths, logs, cost, and version drift.

00:01:30.682 --> 00:01:35.401
Adopt hybrid placement where the combined value exceeds that complexity.

00:01:35.401 --> 00:01:43.402
The aim is to use local control and cloud flexibility selectively, while preserving a coherent service for users.
